description:
**HR Generalist — IBEES** 




**Location:** 
 On\-site (Delhi)




**Experience:** 
 6–8 years




**Industry:** 
 Brand Communication / Advertising / Digital \& Offline Marketing




**Employment Type:** 
 Full\-time




 IBEES is a brand communications agency offering integrated
 **offline and digital solutions** 
 . We are looking for a mature, hands\-on
 **HR Generalist** 
 who can independently manage the employee lifecycle while helping us strengthen recruitment, performance, learning, culture and people practices.




 This is not intended to be a purely administrative HR role. We are looking for someone who can combine
 **strong execution with sound HR judgement** 
 , work closely with business and creative teams, and build practical people processes suited to a fast\-moving agency environment.




**Key Responsibilities** 



* Own the
 **end\-to\-end recruitment process** 
 across creative, digital, client servicing, media, strategy, operations and support functions.
* Partner with department heads to understand manpower requirements, define role expectations, improve hiring quality and reduce time\-to\-fill.
* Build and maintain structured talent pipelines through job portals, referrals, networking and other relevant sourcing channels.
* Manage the complete
 **employee lifecycle** 
 including onboarding, confirmation, transfers, documentation, engagement, grievance handling and exits.
* Drive a structured
 **Performance Management System (PMS)** 
 including KRAs, KPIs, goal\-setting, review cycles, performance discussions, calibration and Performance Improvement Plans where required.
* Work with managers to improve the quality of performance conversations and ensure that appraisals are evidence\-based and aligned with business objectives.
* Identify capability gaps through
 **Training Needs Analysis** 
 and develop practical learning and development initiatives for employees and managers.
* Create and maintain an annual training calendar covering functional, behavioural, managerial and leadership development requirements.
* Build an engaging and accountable
 **company culture** 
 through employee communication, recognition, feedback mechanisms, engagement initiatives and manager sensitisation.
* Conduct employee pulse checks, one\-to\-one discussions, exit interviews and other feedback exercises to identify people issues early.
* Analyse attrition, absenteeism, hiring effectiveness, training effectiveness, employee engagement and other relevant HR metrics.
* Support payroll inputs, attendance, leave, benefits administration, statutory compliance and employee records in coordination with finance/accounts or external partners.
* Review and strengthen HR policies, SOPs, employee handbook practices and internal processes as the organisation grows.
* Maintain strong employee relations while handling grievances and sensitive matters with maturity, confidentiality and fairness.
* Build useful HR dashboards and MIS for management covering headcount, recruitment, attrition, performance, engagement and other key people metrics.
* Act as a trusted HR partner to management while remaining approachable and credible with employees.



**Recruitment Expectations** 




 The person should be comfortable hiring for a diverse agency workforce, which may include roles such as:




**Creative, Copywriting, Graphic Design, Digital Marketing, Performance Marketing, Social Media, Client Servicing, Media, Strategy, Content, Video, Business Development, Operations, Finance and Administration.** 




 Experience hiring for advertising, digital, media, communications, creative services, marketing or other fast\-paced service businesses would be an advantage.




**Performance Management** 




 A major part of this role will be strengthening the performance culture at IBEES. The candidate should be capable of:



* translating business objectives into departmental and individual KRAs;
* defining measurable KPIs;
* creating appraisal calendars and review processes;
* helping managers conduct meaningful reviews;
* driving mid\-year and annual performance discussions;
* managing rating calibration;
* identifying high performers and development needs;
* supporting PIPs for underperformance;
* connecting performance outcomes with development, recognition and career progression.



**Learning \& Development** 




 The HR Generalist will be expected to move beyond organising training programmes and develop a more structured learning framework.




 Responsibilities will include:



* Training Needs Analysis;
* competency\-gap identification;
* employee development plans;
* induction and orientation;
* functional and behavioural training;
* manager\-development programmes;
* external trainer/vendor coordination;
* training feedback and effectiveness measurement.



**Culture \& Employee Engagement** 




 IBEES is looking for someone who understands that
 **culture is more than events and celebrations** 
 .




 The role should help strengthen:



* accountability;
* collaboration;
* recognition;
* communication;
* trust;
* manager effectiveness;
* employee experience;
* ownership and performance orientation.



 Employee engagement programmes, town halls, recognition initiatives, feedback mechanisms and internal communication should support these larger cultural objectives.




**AI \& Technology Orientation — Added Advantage** 




 We would particularly value a candidate who is curious about technology and understands how
 **AI and automation can improve HR productivity and decision\-making** 
 .




 Hands\-on technical expertise is not mandatory, but the candidate should ideally be comfortable exploring tools for:



* AI\-assisted resume screening and sourcing;
* job\-description creation;
* interview\-question generation;
* candidate communication;
* onboarding automation;
* HR helpdesks/chatbots;
* employee surveys and sentiment analysis;
* HR dashboards and analytics;
* training\-content development;
* PMS tracking;
* workflow automation;
* HRMS and ATS platforms.



 Familiarity with tools such as
 **ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot, Gemini, Canva AI, HRMS/ATS systems, Excel/Google Sheets and automation platforms** 
 would be an advantage.




 Most importantly, the individual should understand that AI is a
 **productivity and decision\-support tool** 
 , while final HR decisions must remain thoughtful, fair and human\-led.




**Candidate Profile** 




 We are looking for someone with:



* **6–8 years of relevant HR experience** 
 ;
* strong hands\-on experience as an HR Generalist, HRBP, HR Manager or similar;
* proven recruitment capability;
* practical experience with PMS;
* exposure to employee engagement and culture\-building;
* experience in learning and development;
* strong employee\-relations and grievance\-handling capability;
* good understanding of HR operations and statutory compliance;
* strong written and verbal communication;
* confidence in dealing with senior management and department heads;
* good Excel/Google Sheets and HR reporting capability;
* ability to work independently and execute without excessive supervision.



 An
 **MBA/PGDM in HR or equivalent HR qualification** 
 would be preferred.




**Preferred Characteristics** 




 The ideal person will be:




**hands\-on, commercially aware, structured, approachable, assertive when necessary, data\-oriented, technology\-curious and comfortable working in a fast\-paced creative environment.** 




 They should be able to switch comfortably between:




**interviewing a candidate in the morning, resolving an employee issue, discussing KRAs with a department head, reviewing an HR dashboard and planning a training programme—all within the same day.** 




**What Success Looks Like in the First 6–12 Months** 




 A successful HR Generalist at IBEES should be able to demonstrate:



* improved recruitment turnaround and quality of hiring;
* a clearly defined PMS with measurable KRAs/KPIs;
* improved quality of manager\-employee performance discussions;
* a structured learning calendar;
* stronger onboarding;
* improved employee engagement and communication;
* reduced regrettable attrition;
* stronger HR documentation and process discipline;
* useful management dashboards;
* increased adoption of technology and AI for appropriate HR workflows.
